               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital course of your patient, a 40-year-old female, admitted on 2015-12-11 due to suspected tubal pregnancy following presentation with acute lower abdominal pain and positive beta-hCG. Transvaginal ultrasound confirmed a right-sided ectopic tubal pregnancy with no intrauterine gestational sac. Given hemodynamic stability, diagnostic laparoscopy was performed, confirming the diagnosis. Due to tubal involvement, a laparoscopic salpingectomy was carried out without intraoperative complications. Postoperative recovery was uneventful; serial beta-hCG levels declined appropriately. The patient was discharged on 2015-12-14 in good general condition. Pain management was ensured with oral analgesia. We recommend follow-up beta-hCG monitoring and gynecological review in 4–6 weeks. Please do not hesitate to contact us should any concerns arise.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
